      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-02-26_WidnesExaminer_art0160" n="art0160">
        <p>00 easy to get the medicine habit. DON'T run to a doctor or start dosing at the first sign of illness. Try a new plan. When your stomach, brain or nerves cry for rest, give them rest instead of medicine. But if you continue to feel dull, drowsy and nervous; if you are suffering from head- aches, dizziness, backache and urinary dis- orders, your kidneys need help and should be treated with Doan's Backache Kidney Pills. With their assistance, with a careful diet, more rest, sleep and outdoor exercise; and by avoiding overwork, worry and ex- cesses; you can soon get back to normal. when there will be no more need of medicine. Doan's Pills do not affect the bowels. They are for the kidneys and bladder only. Judge by the honest heartfelt testimony of your own neighbours here in Warrington. Send for Free Book on " Moderation, Cheer- fulness, add Other Long Life Laws."</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON PROOF. On September 11th, 1905, Mr- T. Rigby, of 121, Church-street, near the Training College for Girls, Warrington, said—' Through having to work in all weathers I became subject to pains in my back, which -.Nere sometimes so bad that I cluldt scarcely get about. I was almost afraid to steop,for it was a difficult matter to straighten myself up again.</p>
        <p>"For three years I took different medi- cines, but with no good results. It was different, however, when I started with Dean's Backache Kidney Pills; they did me good from the first, and brought me back to health. lam thankful for the benefit I derived from Beau's Pills, and shall do all I can to make them more widely known." (Signed) "T. Rigby:* On March 12th, 1915—over nine years later —Mr. Rigby said: "Bean's Fills did me last- ing good, and I have nothing to complain of so far as my health is concerned now." Be sure you ask ter DOAN'S and' get DOAN'S—the Pitts Mr. Rigby had. AU dealers, or 210 a box from Foster-McClellan Co., 8, Wells St., Oxford St., London. Tif:</p>
