        <p>PRINTATE S. ITANKINSON. Killed in Action. •</p>
        <p>aunt, Mrs. Agnes Kinder, of 22, A.therton-street. Bank Quay, his own Parents living in Welling- ton, Salop. Twenty years of age, he enlisted in: His Majesty's Forces. 12 Months last September, - being eventually drafted to the Front in "July, 1915. He was familiarly known to his associates as Sam Kinder on account of his residing so long With his aunt. In civilian life he .Was employed at Messrs. Monks, . Hall. and ,Co..:Ltd. (Rivet Department), 'where he was highly esteemed and admired. Ile worshipped *at the Working Men's :1_ Mission, .TheWlis-street, and. as a, boy received his educe-</p>
